SUMMARY:Instagram: Reel: Your job ad and the law (for clinics)
DESCRIPTION:Platform: Instagram\nType: Reel. Show in profile grid: OFF\nFi
 le: design/social-and-merch/instagram-guides/law-reel.mp4 · cover design
 /social-and-merch/instagram-guides/law-reel-cover.jpg (Edit cover\, Add f
 rom camera roll)\nLocation: Canada\nShare to LinkedIn too.\n\nCAPTION:\nH
 iring in Ontario or BC? Your job ad has rules.\n\nOntario\, for employers
  with 25 or more employees\, since 1st January 2026: show the pay range (
 no more than $50\,000 wide)\, say whether it's an existing vacancy\, say 
 whether you use AI to screen applicants\, and don't ask for "Canadian exp
 erience".\n\nBritish Columbia\, all employers: show the pay range in ever
 y public job posting.\n\nOn Kestrel Eye Care Jobs\, every post covers all
  of this\, whatever the size of your clinic. Save this for your next hire
 .\n\nPre launch is open. Set up your clinic: link in bio.\n\nA plain summ
 ary\, not legal advice.\n\n#Hiring #ClinicOwner #Optometry #PayTransparen
 cy #OntarioJobs\n\nALT TEXT:\nA short checklist animation for clinics. Te
 xt reads: What your job ad needs. Ontario\, employers with 25 or more emp
 loyees\, since 1st January 2026: the pay range\, no more than $50\,000 wi
 de\; whether it's an existing vacancy\; whether AI is used to screen appl
 icants\; no Canadian experience requirement. British Columbia\, all emplo
 yers: the pay range in every public job posting. Then: On Kestrel\, every
  post covers all of this\, whatever the size of your clinic. A plain summ
 ary\, not legal advice.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Post now: Instagram\, Reel: Your job ad and the law (for clini
 cs)
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
